## 12. Compensation Review and Salary Adjustments

### 12.1 Annual Salary Review Cycle

Salary reviews are conducted as part of the annual performance review process:

**Timing:**
- Performance reviews conducted: October–December
- Salary decisions communicated: December–January
- Salary increases effective: April 1 each year

**Factors Considered:**
- Performance rating (40% weight)
- Market rate for role and experience level (30% weight)
- Internal equity (20% weight)
- Business performance and budget (10% weight)

### 12.2 Salary Increase Guidelines

**Performance Rating:**
- 4–5 (Exceptional/Strong): 8–12% increase
- 3 (Meets Expectations): 2–5% increase (or 0% if already above market)
- 2 or below (Needs Improvement): 0% increase; may be on performance plan

**Market-Based Adjustment:**
- If employee is significantly below market rate, increase may be 10–15% regardless of performance (to bring closer to market)
- If employee is above market rate, increase may be minimal or 0% (even with strong performance)

**Budget Constraints:**
- If company revenue is down or economic conditions challenging, increases may be smaller (e.g., 3–5% vs. 8–12%)
- This is communicated transparently to all employees

### 12.3 Promotion and Role Change

When an employee is promoted or takes on a significantly different role:
- New salary is typically 10–15% above previous salary
- Tied to new role requirements and market rate
- Effective immediately upon promotion (not waiting for April 1)

### 12.4 Pay Equity and Transparency

BrightPath commits to pay equity:
- Men and women in similar roles with similar experience and performance are paid similarly
- Employees can discuss compensation with peers and manager (not forbidden)
- Compensation decisions are documented and reviewed for equity
- Regular pay equity audits are conducted

